I've got colour IBMgraphics working on OpenBSD i386 on the console.  I'm
thinking of writing up a mini nethack/IBMgraphics/unix/console howto, but
if anyone wants to get it working sooner let me know.

It may or may not work on non-i386 platforms.  (WSDISPLAYIO_USEFONT ioctl
must be supported by the video driver.)

note:  you'll have to patch your kernel or install current CVS to get it
working in OpenBSD on an 80x25 console.  Yes, that's correct: thanks to
nethack, I found an OpenBSD kernel bug :)

